its place well I think that they are  discovering the great foibles of  communism and have developed some  entrepreneurial system that operates  within it and I have always believed  that communism is losing ideology and  that we are all the same and that the  Chinese people would just as everybody  else like to make decisions about their  own lives and this question and what you  notice skip to the to the former Soviet  Union and women what do you see as the  biggest challenge for women in the  former Soviet Union well one of the  interesting things was you know the  communist ideology always said that it  had liberated women that is true they  liberated them to work four times as  hard as the men and they I spent a lot  of time in doing surveys and things  about women and former communist  countries and I think they really felt  that they had not had an opportunity to  have normal lives of any kind and  interestingly enough many of the Soviet  era women then then were Russians or  another nationalities wanted to go and  have a normal life they wanted to be  married they wanted to have children  they they wanted to be able to have jobs  of their choice and so I think those  continue to be their challenges high  time is drawn to a close but I've got to  ask you about your famous hats when you  were secretary of state you were always  wearing a different large often floppy  hat you still do that I do I try not to  look like a mushroom but I do like to  wear hats and the reason it all started  was my daughter picked us up because I  got off a plane on my first trips i love  Stetsons and so I had one and she said  mom I know why you're doing this your  hair was a mess when you woke up in the  morning on that airplane and she was  absolutely right but then it kind of  became a standard and people wanted to  know why I wasn't wearing a hat so the  combination of what kind of pin I was  wearing and what kind of hat I was  wearing goes back to your first question  which is I didn't want to be boring a  secretary of state and you never were  and when it comes to a bed  hair day I sit with that I know exactly  how you feel secretary Madeleine  Albright thank you very much for being  with us  Madam Secretary is published by miramax  books an imprint of Hyperion visit  Hyperion Books com for more information
 

